WEBVTT

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:30.880
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS, YOUR PLAYER IS NOT RENDERING THE SUBTITLES PROPERLY. PLEASE REFER TO http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback FOR THE INTENDED PLAYBACK.}

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.070
He has been promoted from Double A today.
 This is the newcomer, Keane.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.990
You guys should know about him too.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:20.410
He was drafted number one by our Indiana Hornets this year;

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.790
he's the golden rookie catcher!

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.750
In no time at all, he's already risen to Triple A!

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.250
So then, I'm sorry, Sanders.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.630
I'll have you moved to the bench.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:38.640
Ball!

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:41.720
Out!

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.570
<i>We've got a three-run lead.</i>

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:52.990
<i>Don't be petty and selfish about how you want to lead!</i>

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:01.040
For the time being, I'll pitch according to your commands.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.160
If you can get us through this inning without any earned runs being scored,

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:08.790
then I will listen to everything you say without complaining from now on.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.300
But if you let them score even one run,

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.170
never try to give me orders again!

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.300
W-What are you saying, Shigeno?

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.390
That's not something you guys can deci-

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.300
Very well.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:23.810
And you, if you lose this bet,

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.440
never talk back to me again.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:33.780
Back home!

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:36.320
Out!

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:38.320
Out!

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.370
To first!

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:43.990
Out! Out!

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.420
<i>A triple play... seriously?</i>

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.790
<i>A triple play... seriously?</i>

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:51.620
Huh? Are you studying stats even when we're on the move, Keane?

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.550
You sure are dedicated.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:03.050
You won't be able to copy him because your brain is only muscle.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.640
What did you say!?

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.720
So it's been a week since Keane joined us, huh?

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:09.640
Yeah.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.390
Thanks to him, we pitchers get to win.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.230
And our runs against stat is improving.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.520
It's really all thanks to the great Mr. Keane.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:31.000
<i>I won the bet.</i>

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.420
<i>Never disobey me again.</i>

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:56.100
As always, the Bats' batting lineup is at its best, and they score three runs in the first inning.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:01.730
In contrast, the Vipers are trying to fight back but they've lost three men to the Bats' starting pitcher, Quezada!

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:04.610
They start their attack this time with their clean-up hitter, Ponds!

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.950
Quezada!

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:15.540
Return the favor for the home run he hit in the last game!

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.330
I'll kick you if you get hit!

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:20.380
We're counting on you, Quezada!

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.550
<i>That was...</i>

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.760
<i>a careless mistake I made.</i>

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:39.020
<i>This time for sure...</i>

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.730
We'll walk this guy.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.070
What!?

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:48.950
According to our win-loss records, Ponds has hit safely five times in eleven at-bats against us.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:52.660
It's the best strategy, especially after that home run in the previous game.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.410
No! But still...

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:58.920
You'll be back on the bench if he hits you again.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:04.880
To ensure they don't score another run, we'll take a chance with the fifth batter next.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.300
Wait, Keane!

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.970
I'll hold him back this time!

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:11.890
Throw away any foolish pride.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:12.970
What?

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:18.640
Or I'll just retreat to the bench if you don't cooperate.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:26.320
Now hitting, number 5: Ponds!

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:34.080
What? They're using an intentional walk strategy again!?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.580
It's only the second inning.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.870
And against the first batter!?

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.120
Hey, hey.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.340
With how Quezada's looking today, surely he can hold down Ponds.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:45.340
He's pitching well.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.340
Hey!

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.420
We don't want to see this sort of play!

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.970
Show the spirit of Memphis!

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:51.590
That's right!

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:52.890
Fight, Quezada!

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:54.890
Go strong, Quezada!

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.310
That's right. Go!

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.310
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:03.690
Ball!

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:09.700
Ball!

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:13.280
Ball!

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.240
Ball four!

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:26.590
Now hitting, number 12: Garland!

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.170
<i>Come!</i>

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.670
<i>We'll take him!</i>

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:35.970
Out!

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:37.430
Out!

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:40.980
<i>Good.</i>

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:41.980
<i>Just as planned.</i>

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:48.530
Now hitting, number 7: Freud!

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.950
<i>With the sixth batter, if we just get some fastballs on the inside corner...</i>

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.740
Strike out!

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.160
Yes!

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.330
Keep the good work up at this pace!

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.710
Nice, Quezada!

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:05.880
Good job!

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.720
Don't worry, Quezada.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:17.470
It's not like your battle against Ponds has ended.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:19.470
That's right.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:22.100
Fight him face-to-face next time.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:24.900
Yeah.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:47.960
Ball!

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.000
Ball four!

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:56.800
Ball!

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:57.800
Ball four!

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:12.070
They're going to walk Ponds every time he comes to bat, huh?

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.740
Even when we're leading by this much?

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.160
That bastard!

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.380
You did it, Quezada!

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:40.390
This is your first shutout this season!

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:41.760
Yeah.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.730
Since Keane joined, Quezada's won two games in a row.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:46.940
It's all thanks to the great Mr. Keane!

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.480
As expected from our golden rookie.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:55.320
It's not a big deal.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:10:01.660
It's easy to get a Minors pitcher to win if you correctly lead him according to the stats.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.250
What!?

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:06.500
Keane!

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.420
Say that again!

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:09.960
Quezada!

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:15.050
It's the truth.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:19.590
Since I joined, this team has actually won six consecutive games without losing.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:22.510
I haven't let any pitcher lose.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:25.180
And on top of that, our runs per game has improved by 0.7.

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:29.900
If you'll excuse me...

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.270
Wait a sec!

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:39.570
Was it necessary to let the guy walk at the end, when we were way in the lead and the game was ours?

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:43.370
What about a pitcher's pride?

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:50.290
It's because you get distracted by worthless feelings like that that you guys can't rise to the top.

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.670
What!?

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:58.840
I don't intend to get carried away and make a mistake due to things like stubbornness or pride ever again.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.510
"Mistake"?

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:05.560
What do you mean, "again"?

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:25.370
I think he was talking about when he was in college.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.580
Miss,

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.290
do you know something?

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.210
Yeah.

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:36.380
Keane has stood out as a player ever since college.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.210
And...

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:45.680
it was when Keane's college, which had many strong players, was trying to qualify for the All-American Tournament.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:53.440
In the state finals, they just needed to be careful with one dangerous batter to win.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:12:00.990
In the final inning, they faced that batter in a situation where he could turn the tables around with one hit.

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:04.410
That's when their pitcher requested challenging him.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:09.370
"I'll hold him back no matter what."

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.370
Believing in his words, Keane entrusted everything to him.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:22.930
As a result, they allowed their opponent to get a winning hit, and Keane's college was eliminated in the state preliminaries.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:32.020
I think it was from that point that his baseball changed.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:40.730
He's been getting results by believing in decisions based solely on statistics.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:43.400
Thoroughly and without giving in.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:59.590
This is a free fansub.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:59.590
Not for sale or rent.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:19.150
<i>Rather than imitating an old man,
concentrate on your fastball more!</i>

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:24.280
<i>If you can gain true control over your serious fastballs,</i>

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.030
<i>you'll be able to strike out even Bolton and Gibson Jr!</i>

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:42.000
<i>Four out of ten pitches.</i>

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.010
<i>I still have a long way to go.</i>

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:48.180
Wow, that's some power.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:03.480
Have you always been practicing by yourself with that iron frame?

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.400
Yeah.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:07.110
That's cold of you.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:10.530
I could have helped you any time if you just asked.

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:11.950
You're one to talk.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:16.620
You're always on your back, fast asleep, and snoring after a game.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:25.590
What do you think of him?

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:30.840
It's true that with Keane's lead you get results.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:36.640
It's effective to attack based on reliable statistics rather than attacking recklessly.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:44.480
It's true that the Bats need Keane more than me.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:54.620
I don't think statistics are everything.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.160
Don't become weak-hearted, old man.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:05.880
Well, I'll go sweat some more and then head back.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:06.630
What?

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:07.920
You're going to continue?

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:09.590
Of course.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:12.340
Unlike you, I have energy to spare.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:13.930
What!?

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:18.850
You go be yourself, hurry off to sleep, and maintain your condition.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:21.770
You never know when another chance will come.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:27.480
Yeah.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:39.290
Today's game between the Kings and the Bats has been at a standstill with a pitching duel. However,

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:43.630
in the top of the ninth inning this stalemate was broken by the Bats, with their fired-up batting, making it 1- 0.

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:49.420
It's now the bottom half of the ninth, with the Kings batting, and one out with no runners.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:56.390
Can the Bats' pitcher, Matt, follow Quezada up and finish this game with a shutout!?

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:06.980
Ball!

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:07.940
Ball four!

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:15.120
<i>He's almost out of breath.</i>

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:21.330
Ball!

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:22.290
Ball four!

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:35.760
Shigeno.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:42.850
Attention please, pitching, number 56:

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:46.270
Goro Shigeno!

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:01.500
We're counting on you, Shigeno.

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:09.800
Shigeno.

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:12.170
We're going to use a bases loaded strategy again.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.550
You mean <i>"again."</i>

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:17.640
Okay.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:23.480
Ball!

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:24.560
Ball four!

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:29.860
Attention please.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:34.740
Batting, number 54: Pedeño!

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:38.120
What!?

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:39.950
Pedeño!?

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:42.580
Time!

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:50.170
Pedeño is a major leaguer who batted clean-up for the Atlanta Fighters.

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:51.920
A major leaguer?

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:55.970
He broke his right wrist and was supposed to be recovering, but...

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:00.260
to think he'd come back to the game already...

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:06.890
He shouldn't be back to his regular condition, but he has power.

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:11.400
We should aim for something low and inside-where he's weak.

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:14.940
That sounds fun.

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:20.490
I hope you haven't forgotten... to never disobey me.

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:23.490
Yeah, I know.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:30.920
Play!

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:01.280
Foul! Foul!

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:03.120
That was close.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.080
Yeah.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:22.470
<i>As expected from you, Pedeño.</i>

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:22.470
Play!

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:25.720
<i>There's no question why he's a first-class batter in the Majors.</i>

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:29.980
<i>Looks like he's worked on his weakness during that short time.</i>

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:34.770
<i>If the statistics up till now won't help here,</i>

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:37.610
<i>throw a ball outside, Shigeno!</i>

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:44.450
What!?

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:51.580
<i>Thanks, Major Leaguer-san,</i>

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.920
<i>for blowing away the statistics.</i>

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:56.800
<i>The same location!?</i>

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:01.800
Foul!

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.050
<i>Did he mistime his swing!?</i>

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:08.560
<i>Thanks to you, I can pitch with ease.</i>

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:15.730
<i>You can't win if you lose mentally!</i>

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:30.410
Strike out!

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:32.080
All right!

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.540
That guy is something.

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:37.710
He beat Pedeño.

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:38.460
Yeah.

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:42.930
Shigeno...

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:51.560
<i>He struck Pedeño out with three pitches in a row to the same location?</i>

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:59.230
Now hitting, number 26: Zenobi!

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:01.530
<i>I see.</i>

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:02.900
Play!

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:08.740
<i>When the opponent is strong, the more he's cornered, the stronger he grows.</i>

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:11.500
<i>He likes fighting power with power.</i>

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:16.500
<i>The more motivated he is, the more the control and speed of his pitching improves. That's the type of player he is.</i>

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:18.500
<i>In that case...</i>

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:21.880
Down the middle?

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.340
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:41.440
Thank you, Shigeno!

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:02.090
Keane!

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:09.180
Stats ain't everything, are they?

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:15.480
No, it just means that there are new stats.

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:16.600
Huh?

00:24:11.800 --> 00:24:14.760
Sanders puts on his catcher's mask after a long time,

00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:19.430
but he's unable to produce good results and make decisions.

00:24:19.980 --> 00:24:22.770
A-Are you serious, old man!?

00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:24.360
Next time, on Major:

00:24:24.360 --> 00:24:25.730
Hero.

00:24:25.730 --> 00:24:28.230
Run to the stage of your dreams!
